# Lean 4 build artifacts (Lake)
.lake/

# `lake-manifest.json` is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It was, and that made the proofs unreproducible. `lakefile.toml` requires
# Mathlib without a revision, so Lake resolves it to `master`. With the
# manifest ignored, a fresh checkout (CI, or a new machine) resolves `master`
# to whatever is newest *at that moment* — not the revision these theorems
# were actually checked against. Mathlib's master moves daily and does not
# stay compatible with a pinned older toolchain, so "the proofs type-check"
# would have meant different things on different days.
#
# The manifest records the exact resolved revision of Mathlib and its
# transitive dependencies. Committing it is what makes `scripts/proof_gate.sh`
# reproducible, and it is what upstream Mathlib and downstream projects do.
# Update it deliberately with `lake update`, then re-run the proof gate.
